// @expect-errors: 1
// @expect-first-at: 16:13

// A Cx keyword used as a function name. `target` is TokenKind.Target,
// so the parser reads it as a `target(...)` declaration and fails to
// find the expected identifier.
//
// This used to crash with a memory access violation (0xC0000005),
// because the failed `consume` returned a symbol token whose union
// field `s` was never initialized and got hashed as a garbage
// pointer. See `Token.s` in frontend/lexer/token.d.
//
// The test pins two things:
//   - it does not crash
//   - it reports exactly one error, at 1:13
void target(){}